Neon spaces (M3), part 3 of 4: two-finger swipe.

A pre-target handler on the tab strip region turns touchpad scrolls over the
sidebar into finger-tracked swipes of the pager: the axis locks after 15 DIP
(a mostly vertical gesture scrolls the tab list), the pages follow the
fingers and resist past the first and last space, and on release they turn
past a third of a page or a fling of 500 DIP/s, else snap back. The end of a
gesture is the platform's lift (macOS phases, a fling start on Wayland and on
X11 with libinput's scroll stop), or a quiet period of 120 ms without one.
A notched sideways wheel turns one page per notch. SpacesSwipeTracker holds
the gesture logic without ui::Event, so a macOS patch can feed it native
phases. No hooks. Neon code, GPL-3.0.

